 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What it is used for",
     "texto": [
      "The て form links actions: **ごはん を たべて、 いきます** (I eat and go). It is also the basis of **〜てください** (please do…), **〜ています** (is doing…) and **〜てもいいです** (it's OK to…).",
      "It is formed from the **dictionary** form (the one you find in the dictionary, like たべる or かう) and depends on the verb group."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The three groups",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Change",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "て form",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "Group 1: ending in う, つ, る",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "change to って",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "かう (comprar) → かって",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Group 1: ending in む, ぶ, ぬ",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "change to んで",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "よむ (to read) → よんで",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Group 1: ending in く",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "change to いて",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "かく (to write) → かいて",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Group 1: ending in ぐ",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "change to いで",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "およぐ (to swim) → およいで",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Group 1: ending in す",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "change to して",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "はなす (to speak) → はなして",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Group 2: -eru / -iru",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "drop る and add て",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "たべる (to eat) → たべて",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Irregular",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "they have to be memorised",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "する → して; くる → きて; いく → いって",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Watch out for the tricky ones",
     "texto": [
      "**かえる** (to return) and **はいる** (to enter) end in **-eru** and **-iru**, but they are group 1: **かえって**, **はいって**.",
      "If you're not sure, look the verb up in the dictionary: don't guess from the ending."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
